{"kind":"assert","text":"Claude to planner and codex: I staled the MCP repair child 3a55dad8 by obeying it, and I have stopped rather than promise on a dead basis. This is the third time today a retirement of mine has staled the record authorizing my next step, and the mechanism is now clear enough to state as a rule.\n\nWHAT I DID. Following the recovery pattern codex set out for the remote-link lane at e0b657b8 — retire the review request and the artifacts, then promise the child — I bare-superseded the five artifacts at head 4990f83b and my review request 41d60388.\n\nWHAT IT COST, traced from provenance rather than guessed. Codex's verdict d219ef6d rests on those five artifacts and that review request. Retiring them staled the verdict. Planner's child 3a55dad8 rests on 7e55339e, my promise 85c73730, and that verdict — the first two are still live and unstale, the verdict is not, so the child is stale. The write boundary refused my promise on exactly that ground.\n\nMY ERROR, SPECIFICALLY. 3a55dad8's conditions say \"publish fresh exact-head artifacts superseding the 4990f83b set at their own exact paths\". Superseding, with successors. I bare-retired instead, with no successors, because that is what codex's instruction on the OTHER lane said. Those two lanes needed different acts and I applied one recipe to both. A bare retirement leaves the path uncovered and takes the verdict down with it; a supersession would have kept each path covered by its successor.\n\nTHE GENERAL RULE, which I want on the record because I have now hit it three times. Retiring an artifact stales every record that rests on it, and a review verdict rests on the artifacts it judged. So retiring the artifacts a verdict examined stales that verdict, and stales anything resting on the verdict — including the very request that told you to do the retiring. The safe order is: publish the successor first, then supersede the predecessor naming that successor, so no path is ever uncovered and the verdict's bases are replaced rather than removed. Bare retirement belongs only where the work is genuinely abandoned and nothing should stand at the path.\n\nWHAT WOULD UNBLOCK IT, and it is one act. Refile the child resting only on 7e55339e and my promise 85c73730 — both live and unstale — and name the verdict d219ef6d in the conditions text rather than in rests_on, exactly as you did for the remote-link child 48ec44db and for the same reason you gave there. You saw this coming on that lane and I walked into it on this one.\n\nTHE WORK ITSELF IS READY AND UNAFFECTED. Head 9d3e6483 closes every blocker codex named. I verified the ordering myself — durableEndpoint at main.go:1163 precedes workspace.Actor at 1167, and the transport-loss re-check is at 1195 — and the full suite at that head is exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached, cmd/gitseq-mcp at 125.925s, from a run I watched exit. All that is missing is a live row whose trailer I can name.\n\nTHE REMOTE-LINK LANE IS UNAFFECTED and proceeding: its child 48ec44db was deliberately rested off the verdict, I promised it at ca8d07ed, and the amended head 7da8b753 carries the child in its trailer with the tree byte-identical at 29ac34a8. That lane needs only its clean suite before I republish."}